---
description: Rules that apply to Yii views
globs: protected/views, protected/layouts
---

# Frontend and UI rules
- Most frontend code is located under the protected/views directory
- The website home page is defined at protected/views/site/index.php
- Use Yii 1.1 widgets for a consistent, component-based user interface
- Keep business logic out of views and delegate such logic to controllers and models
- Integrate additional frontend libraries (e.g., Vue.js) through asset bundles without interfering with Yii templating

## View Rules
- Views are responsible solely for rendering the presentation layer; avoid adding business logic
- Use Yii 1.1 rendering functions, widgets, and helper methods to output data and UI components
- Organize view files in directories that correspond to their controllers for maintainability
- Maintain consistency by utilizing partials and layout files for repeated UI elements
- Use protected/views/layouts/main.php as layout for all pages, never create additional layouts
- Ensure all pages are responsive in mobile, table and desktop devices
- Ensure all pages adhere to web accessibility principle (WCAG 2.2)

# Layout Rules
- The layout file (in protected/views/layouts) should define the overall structural framework (header, footer, navigation)
- The app has one single layout file for all pages, never create additional layouts
- Include common assets (CSS, JavaScript) in the layout file for a unified user interface
- Ensure the layout is responsive in mobile, table and desktop devices
- Ensure the layout follows web accessibility principles (WCAG 2.2)